<title>BELGIUM: EU vets John Deere/Lombard deal.</title>
<headline>EU vets John Deere/Lombard deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it was starting a routine probe into a deal by which John Deere Capital Corporation, controlled by Deere &amp; Company of the U.S., and Lombard North Central Plc share control in John Deere Credit Ltd.</p>
<p>Lombard North Central is a subsidiary of National Westminster Bank Plc. John Deere Capital Corp makes and distributes farm and other equipment.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement the deal could apparently fall under the European Union's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions in the EU.</p>
<p>It has about a month to clear the operation or start an in-depth, four-month, inquiry. Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
